{
  "about": [
    "What every SCE payload reader refuses, and how it names the refusal,",
    "written out by hand (docs/adr/0087, sections 2.3 and 2.4).",
    "",
    "A reader that refuses an event's data says why in a sentence each runtime",
    "spells in its own words, and beside the sentence carries the refusal as",
    "data: a code of sce:std/lift/refusal_code.scxml, the place as a strict",
    "RFC 6901 pointer (empty for the whole text, otherwise `/` before each",
    "reference token, `~` written `~0` and `/` written `~1`), and the bound the",
    "value broke for `tooLong` (bytes), `tooMany` (elements) and `tooFew` (the",
    "lower count, elements), null for every other code. The sentences are not compared here; the data is, so that one",
    "text is one refusal on every runtime.",
    "",
    "Why a shared table: read in their code on 2026-11-04, the readers disagreed",
    "on what a text is. Python's `json.loads` and Go's `encoding/json` kept the",
    "last value of a repeated name, the C and C++ readers the first, and the",
    "Rust, Kotlin and Swift readers refused it; and the C reader wrote the byte",
    "a `\\u0000` escape names into a text it holds NUL-terminated, where the",
    "text ends. A table read by every reader is what holds them to one answer.",
    "",
    "Each case gives `data`, the event's data as it arrives; `type`, the type of",
    "its one field `v`, in the form the Interpreter's reader takes",
    "(`\"uint8\"`, `\"string\"` for a text with no bound, `[\"low\", \"high\"]` for",
    "an enum, `{\"string\": B}`, `{\"bytes\": B}`, `{\"optional\": T}`,",
    "`{\"list\": T, \"max\": B}` with `\"min\": M` beside it for a list that",
    "states a lower count (docs/adr/0086, section 15), `{\"record\": {\"id\": T}}`,",
    "`{\"union\": {\"tag\": K, \"cases\": {\"name\": null or {\"record\": ...}}}}`",
    "for a union whose tag stands under the key K, its enum the cases' names, an",
    "empty case `null` (docs/adr/0092, section 4); a reader reads the tag first,",
    "then the record of the case it names from the same object);",
    "and either",
    "`refusal`, what the reader must refuse the data with, or `accepted: true`",
    "for data the reader must read. A record's fields are read in the order the",
    "table writes them, and no case depends on that order. The bounds are 2, 3",
    "and 8, so a reader whose bounds are fixed when it is compiled reads every",
    "case through one instance per bound.",
    "",
    "A text is JSON by RFC 8259 alone on every reader: whitespace of the four",
    "kinds between tokens, a number in its grammar (no leading zero, no `+`, a",
    "digit on each side of `.` and after an exponent), no raw control character",
    "in a text, no half of a UTF-16 pair in a `\\u` escape. Read on 2026-11-04,",
    "the Rust and Kotlin readers took `01` and `1.`, a raw control character and",
    "a lone surrogate, Python's and Go's took a lone surrogate, the C and C++",
    "readers a raw control character, and every reader `-0` for an integer.",
    "",
    "A case that gives `depth` is read as a `<sce:lift>` reads a text",
    "(docs/adr/0087, section 2.1): a record whose one field is `v`, `depth` the",
    "deepest container a value of it holds. Before the text is read as JSON, a",
    "text that is empty or only whitespace is `notJson`, and a container opened",
    "deeper than `depth` is `tooDeep`, decided over the text's brackets alone",
    "(a text skipped from its quote to the next quote no backslash escapes),",
    "its bound `depth`. Its pointer names the container refused: for each",
    "container it stands in, outermost first, the element's index in an array",
    "(the commas met at that level since the array opened) or the member's name",
    "in an object (the last text closed at that level before a colon, since the",
    "object opened or its last comma). The pointer stops before the first place",
    "it cannot write: a member with no name before its colon, a name that is no",
    "text (no JSON string, or holding U+0000), or a token that would take it",
    "past `pathBound` UTF-8 bytes, the room of the refusal record's `path`: 256,",
    "the standard refusal's, where a case gives none."
  ],
